            "Corporate general ledger accounting under Circular 99/2025/TT-BTC: monthly payroll expenses must be categorized functionally by operational department — debiting Account 642 for executive administrative personnel, Account 641 for sales teams, and Account 622 for direct manufacturing labor — rather than aggregated under the name of the disbursement bank. Compensation expenses accrue during the performance period; outstanding employee obligations are recognized under Account 334 (Payables to employees) until final bank disbursement. This accounting interpretation is an unofficial summary of Circular 99/2025/TT-BTC for educational illustration.",
            "Statutory social insurance, health insurance, and personal income tax withholdings represent employee property held in fiduciary trust: the enterprise credits Account 338 (Other payables, sub-accounts 3383, 3384, 3386) and Account 3335 (Personal income tax payable). These withholdings represent pass-through liabilities, never corporate operating expenses or revenues. Mandatory employer-paid insurance contributions represent separate corporate payroll tax expenses not modeled in this simplified scenario.",
            "Commercial banking institutions maintain specialized charts of accounts prescribed for licensed credit institutions rather than Circular 99/2025/TT-BTC. Conceptually: customer checking balances constitute demand deposit liabilities; intra-bank On-Us payroll execution debits employer corporate deposit liabilities and credits employee personal deposit liabilities. Off-Us execution debits employer deposits and credits interbank clearing settlement accounts. Bank account numerical codes are intentionally omitted.",
            "On corporate ledgers, both On-Us and Off-Us salary disbursements are recognized via an identical Credit entry to Account 112 (Demand deposits) upon settlement debit confirmation from the bank. Certain enterprises track pending batch payment files using Account 113 (Cash in transit); our core reference model executes direct debit entries upon statement verification.",
