                "Crucially, from the commercial bank's treasury perspective, zero money departed the building. The bank's aggregated pool of low-cost [[CASA|casa]] deposits remains exactly one hundred percent intact. The bank simply changed the name of the creditor to whom it owes 20 million VND.",
                "Because intra-bank transfers require zero external liquidity reserves and carry zero interbank settlement risk, commercial banks have offered them free of charge for over a decade. It is pure internal bookkeeping, analogous to moving money between two internal envelopes without ever stepping outside your front door."
